  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Index-Card File",
    "overview": "SupportDesk AI is a support desk kept like a well-ordered card file on a beige desk. Every ticket is a card of warm card stock with a violet header rule; every SLA clock is a rubber date-stamp pressed slightly off-square; and one Electric Lemon highlighter marks the only places that say \"act here\". The world is paper, ink and stamp, not glass and gradients: surfaces are flat, separated by hairline rules, and the only lift belongs to things that float over the desk (sheets, dialogs, the fanned cards on the welcome screen).\n\nDensity is set for an agent working a queue all shift: 4dp cells, 48dp touch targets, compact labels, and a single family carrying everything from the 34px display line to 11px stamp text. The customer screens use the same vocabulary at a calmer pace, so a stamp reading \"Due 45m\" means the same thing to the customer and to the agent answering them. The system explicitly refuses the navy-and-teal SaaS card kit with gradient stat tiles. It is light only, on the pinned Porcelain Beige ground.\n\nThe embeddable web chat widget (`frontend/front.html`) carries the same palette, family, radii and bubble language as CSS custom properties, so the customer meets the same desk on the web.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Porcelain Beige desk ground, card-stock paper surfaces, hairline rules.",
      "Violet stamp ink: Heather Purple for fills, icons and rules; Violet Ink for anything that must be read.",
      "One Electric Lemon highlighter, reserved for the primary action and things waiting on the user.",
      "Schibsted Grotesk only, proportional figures throughout.",
      "Elevation is a hairline border or a shadow, never both.",
      "The SLA stamp is the signature: a double-ruled, tilted rubber stamp with four states."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Highlighter Rule",
        "body": "Electric Lemon means \"act here\" and nothing else: the primary action (one per screen state) and things waiting on the user (unread, attention counts, at-risk SLA). It is never decoration, never a brand stripe, never a chart series.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Ink-Not-Heather Rule",
        "body": "Heather Purple (#9B7ED6) is never used for text; at 3.2:1 on paper it is fill, icon and rule only. Any violet text uses Violet Ink.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Family Rule",
        "body": "Schibsted Grotesk is the only typeface, in the app and the web widget. No second display face, no mono.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Proportional Figures Rule",
        "body": "No `tabular-nums` (`fontVariant`/`font-variant-numeric`) anywhere: this face widens punctuation with it. Ids, times and counts use the Numeric role at weight 600 instead.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Border-Or-Shadow Rule",
        "body": "Elevation is declared once per element: a hairline border or a shadow, never both. Cards, chips, inputs and bars use a border; dialogs and sheets use the shadow.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** use Electric Lemon (#E4FF3B) only for the primary action (one per screen state) and things waiting on the user.",
      "**Do** set violet text in Violet Ink (#4A3290); keep Heather Purple (#9B7ED6) for fills, icons and rules.",
      "**Do** use Schibsted Grotesk for everything, with each role naming its own weight file on Android.",
      "**Do** give every element either a 1px Rule border or `ELEVATION.raised`, choosing by whether it sits on the desk or floats above it.",
      "**Do** show SLA time with the SLA stamp in its four states (safe, at-risk, breached, done).",
      "**Do** keep spacing on the 4dp grid and touch targets at 48dp or more.",
      "**Do** take status, priority and channel colours from their fixed triples in `src/theme/colors.js`."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** set any text in Heather Purple.",
      "**Don't** use Electric Lemon as decoration, a brand band or a chart series; analytics bars are Heather Purple.",
      "**Don't** add a second typeface or a mono face.",
      "**Don't** turn on `tabular-nums`.",
      "**Don't** combine a border and a shadow on one element.",
      "**Don't** use the navy-and-teal SaaS kit or gradient stat tiles.",
      "**Don't** add a dark theme; the ground is pinned Porcelain Beige."
    ]
  }
